tests: prove fairness backlog for every small-request interval

Issue #4 fairness measurement closure.

Capacity, target generations and cumulative admissions now come from one
complete strictly parsed listcs reply. Capacity is conservatively bounded by
sum(max(current,maxJobs)) so a lowered advertised ceiling cannot make the proof
easier.

Each of the ten small requests is proven individually. With monotone admission
and reply counters, admitted_before - replies_after is a lower bound throughout
the request interval; requiring it above the shared farm-capacity bound excludes
the endpoint-rebound gap. Topology and target connection generations must remain
stable.

A pure arithmetic fixture retains the endpoint-rebound counterexample, and the
historical endpoint-only mutant must fail at that named trace. The integration
gate reports maximum reply budgets and minimum proven margins.
